      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, I wouldn't recommend using salt tablets or concentrated saltwater. Saline or salt tablets should only be taken under the guidance of a healthcare professional and with proper dosing. Crushing a salt tablet and putting it in water can be toxic and lead to an imbalance of electrolytes, especially for a child. It's better to stick to the oral rehydration solution I mentioned earlier or follow the advice of a pediatrician or healthcare provider for the best and safest solution.",
